WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Speaker 1: Well, the economic situation in the&nbsp;
United States has taken a very interesting turn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.760
And in particular, if you believe, as I believe&nbsp;
the evidence shows, that one of the greatest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:15.760
indicators as to how a particular election is&nbsp;
going to go is the perception of how the economy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:21.920
is doing. Things are all of a sudden looking quite&nbsp;
okay for Democrats and not so good for Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.000
if the average person actually understands what's&nbsp;
going on. And I want to start by looking at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.240
first interesting indicator for today, and that&nbsp;
is gas prices. Gas prices have now continued to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:43.440
fall for nearly 60 days in a row and are below $4&nbsp;
per gallon for the first time since March of 2022.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:50.000
Now, why are gas prices so important? Because&nbsp;
this is our is gasoline really a major expense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.840
for most households? And the answer is not&nbsp;
directly. Certainly, if you're in transportation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:02.640
Uber drivers, etc., it's a major thing. If you&nbsp;
have a long commute, it's a major thing. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.160
there's two reasons why this is important. Number&nbsp;
one, many people look at gas prices as a general&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.600
proxy towards are things cheaper, expensive&nbsp;
right now. And when gas is 502 per gallon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.720
as it was two months ago, there is the perception&nbsp;
that things are generally expensive. And when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.120
gas now drops below $4 a gallon, there's the&nbsp;
perception that things are cheaper. We know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.440
things are cheaper because inflation has started&nbsp;
to come down. But there's another issue with gas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:33.280
prices, which is so many of the things that we&nbsp;
depend on, food products of different kinds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.800
so many different things, they come on trucks&nbsp;
and are affected by gas prices as well. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.760
this is an important indicator for that reason.&nbsp;
And when we look at the GasBuddy price charts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:50.000
you will see that there was this peak at about&nbsp;
502 per gallon late in actually early in June. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.680
then it has been a continued and steady decline&nbsp;
now below $4 per gallon to what looks like let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:03.200
me see officially what CNN says, 399 per gallon as&nbsp;
of this morning, according to Triple A. So let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.880
now take a deeper look at some of these economic&nbsp;
indicators. If you step back and you think about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.840
over the last two weeks, what have we seen? Well,&nbsp;
we've seen the stock market increase nicely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:20.000
We've seen a blockbuster jobs report where&nbsp;
a quarter of a million jobs were expected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.480
in July and we got over 500,000 jobs, more than&nbsp;
doubling the expectation. Inflation is down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:33.840
Gas prices are down. The Inflation Reduction Act&nbsp;
has been signed. The pack or with the Inflation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:40.240
Reduction Act has been voted approved by the&nbsp;
Senate, and then tomorrow presumably will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:45.760
approved by the House and very quickly signed&nbsp;
by Joe Biden. The PACT Act has been signed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.480
Wages are up. And then on the other hand, you have&nbsp;
Donald Trump raided by the FBI with pictures of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.760
his toilet, with documents in it circulating as&nbsp;
he pled the fifth yesterday, more than 400 times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:03.280
when deposed by the New York attorney general.&nbsp;
Things aren't looking very good for trumpworld&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:10.400
and things are looking increasingly good for a Joe&nbsp;
Biden. Now, is it good that gas prices are low?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:18.880
One of the things that we have to understand&nbsp;
is that it's not necessarily good for the long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.880
term for gas to be so cheap in the&nbsp;
United States. I have said before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.240
gasoline prices in the United States are&nbsp;
not accurate in the sense of representing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.440
the true cost of a gallon of gas, particularly&nbsp;
including the environmental cost of a gallon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:40.400
of gas. When gas is more expensive, people tend&nbsp;
to use less of it. And when you look at Europe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:46.400
you see smaller vehicles and people being much&nbsp;
more judicious in terms of their road trips.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.840
I've done road trips and done extensive&nbsp;
driving and we think now Spain, France,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:04:01.280
Italy. At minimum, if not other places as well.&nbsp;
And with tiny vehicles, I mean, tiny vehicles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.880
compact cars, little stick shift, compact cars&nbsp;
that I rent. It's stunning when I don't drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:13.360
that much. And the gas bill is €70. And if in&nbsp;
the United States, gas prices were similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.920
those in Europe, which are arguably more accurate&nbsp;
in representing the true cost of a gallon of gas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.400
people would drive a lot less and we would be&nbsp;
doing less damage to the environment. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:27.920
while by traditional economic standards,&nbsp;
inflation down, gas prices down, stocks up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:34.960
all of this stuff looks good for Biden. I&nbsp;
also am painfully aware of the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.760
higher gas prices encourage people to get off of&nbsp;
gas powered vehicles and move over to electrics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:44.720
to drive less, to look for a more fuel efficient&nbsp;
vehicles. So these are all double edged swords,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:50.880
but by the standard indicators we look at, things&nbsp;
are looking really good. Doesn't mean there isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.080
poverty, inequality, lack of access to health&nbsp;
care. Of course, we haven't solved the economy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.360
overnight, but many of the indicators Republican&nbsp;
themselves look at are looking very, very good.

